# Security headers — brand InfoSec / vendor-scan readiness.
# CSP is REPORT-ONLY on purpose (2026-07-27). Browsers never block on it, so this cannot
# break the map or the tour widgets — it only reports what an enforced policy WOULD block.
# Two reasons it is not enforced yet:
#   1. The app is ~10 inline <script> blocks, so script-src needs 'unsafe-inline' until
#      those are moved out or nonced — which removes most of CSP's real value.
#   2. ~60 third-party origins are referenced (tour widgets, tiles, photo hosts, telemetry)
#      and many load only on specific tabs, so an enforced policy guessed wrong = broken app.
# Origins below were MEASURED off the live site, not guessed. Before flipping this to the
# enforcing `Content-Security-Policy`, exercise every tab and confirm zero violation reports.
# ⚠ frame-ancestors stays permissive — the app is an intentionally embeddable widget.
# No X-Frame-Options: the app is an intentionally embeddable widget (hotels embed it).
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(self), camera=(self), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors *; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' 'unsafe-eval' https://js.sentry-cdn.com https://challenges.cloudflare.com https://widget.getyourguide.com https://www.viator.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; font-src 'self' data:; img-src 'self' data: blob: https:; connect-src 'self' https://api.open-meteo.com https://*.supabase.co https://*.workers.dev https://*.i.posthog.com https://*.ingest.us.sentry.io https://world.openbeautyfacts.org; frame-src https://challenges.cloudflare.com https://widget.getyourguide.com https://www.viator.com https://partners.booking.com https://www.google.com https://maps.google.com; worker-src 'self' blob:; manifest-src 'self'
  # Allow large image previews in Search / Discover (thumbnail-size directive; does NOT force indexing).
  X-Robots-Tag: max-image-preview:large

# ── /d/<token> partner dashboard — ENFORCING CSP (2026-08-10) ────────────────
# This surface is the exception to the report-only policy above, and it earns an
# enforced policy for one reason: the token in the URL path IS the credential.
# Unlike index.html, /d/ loads only four origins (measured, not guessed):
# supabase (REST + Edge Functions + storage), Google Fonts, jsdelivr, self.
# No tour widgets, no tiles, no telemetry — so there is nothing here to break.
#
# The real protection is connect-src: even if the jsdelivr bundle were swapped,
# the injected code could not POST the dashboard token to an attacker origin.
# script-src still needs 'unsafe-inline' (1 inline block + 6 on* handlers), so
# this policy is exfiltration containment, NOT inline-XSS prevention. Removing
# those handlers would let 'unsafe-inline' drop and close that gap.
# frame-ancestors 'none': the operator dashboard is never embedded (unlike the
# guest app, which stays framable above).
/d/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://cdn.jsdelivr.net; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data: blob: https://arndnljtmjfsnzcpcuen.supabase.co; connect-src 'self' https://arndnljtmjfsnzcpcuen.supabase.co
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
/d.html
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://cdn.jsdelivr.net; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data: blob: https://arndnljtmjfsnzcpcuen.supabase.co; connect-src 'self' https://arndnljtmjfsnzcpcuen.supabase.co
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer

# ── Operator Dashboard: not embeddable ──────────────────────────────────────
# One file (dashboard.html) served at five clean routes. Unlike the guest app above,
# which is deliberately framable because hotels embed it, the operator Dashboard is a
# signed-in surface and has no reason to appear inside anyone else's page. It DOES
# frame /portal-demo/ itself, so 'self' rather than 'none'.
# X-Frame-Options is the belt for clients that predate frame-ancestors.
/dashboard.html
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'self'
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow
/hotel
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'self'
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow
/timeshare
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'self'
